  "source": "Tower A (rigid D1, joint masses only): masses and centres of mass by statics (x weighted by the Y masses, y by the X masses; cumulative from the story up); centres of rigidity from the 6 x 6 stiffness of the two levels' UX, UY, RZ (cantilever columns joined only by the diaphragm, as B58), a unit Fx, Fy or Mz on one level with the other free: XCR = -theta(Fy)/theta(Mz), YCR = theta(Fx)/theta(Mz); WCM solved on the same stiffness with each row at its level's centre of mass. Tower C (semi-rigid SR1): the centre of mass of its joint masses, masses 0; base shears equal the loads.",
